{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoF4Vef61ATNv5niozym","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added `TTLCache` in `ledgerkit/cache.py` and its tests in `tests/test_cache.py`, and committed both as e2b2dc6 on `crew/1107-616f79`. `python3 -m pytest -q` reports 10 passed, covering the existing `test_money.py` and the new cache tests.\n\nThe cache follows your spec. Details worth knowing:\n- **Locking:** every method takes an `RLock`, which makes it safe under concurrent threads.\n- **Cost of the expiry sweep:** `put` of a new key and `__len__` scan all entries to drop expired ones, so they are O(n) in the number of entries. That is fine at small sizes but would be slow for very large caches.\n- **Thread-safety test:** it runs 8 threads of mixed `put`, `get` and `len` calls. It checks that the cache stays within `maxsize` and that hits plus misses add up. It is a smoke test, not proof that there are no races.\n\nI did not push anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2388,"cache_read_input_tokens":31725,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2388},"output_tokens":325,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f47ee1d8-15f0-449e-b5ed-7d61da7fd04c","uuid":"ba27ab1e-e11d-42a8-9011-99a9476b4f34","timestamp":"2026-11-07T08:21:38.885Z","request_id":"req_011CgoF4VRXaGSErF82zcvb9"}
